   1          /* =============================================================================
   2             File: rx_ecc.c
   3             Module: Group 3 -- Error Correction (PESEC + H1 + SEC+DED)
   4          
   5             Implementation of:
   6               - PESEC matrix construction (mirroring the TX encoder)
   7               - PESEC syndrome computation and single-bit error correction
   8               - [W4] SEC+DED overall parity check for double-error detection
   9               - H1 differential state tracking (secondary validation layer)
  10          
  11             SEC+DED UPGRADE (W4):
  12               rx_pesec_correct() now accepts an overall_parity parameter.  The
  13               TX computes P = parity(data[14:0]) XOR parity(red[9:0]) and shifts
  14               it out as the 26th bus bit.  The RX recomputes parity locally and
  15               compares it with the received P.  Combined with the PESEC syndrome,
  16               this yields a 4-case truth table:
  17          
  18                 Syndrome | Parity Check | Meaning
  19                 ---------|--------------|------------------------------------------
  20                   == 0   |     OK       | No error (PESEC_NO_ERROR)
  21                   != 0   |     FAIL     | Single error -> correct (PESEC_CORRECTED_*)
  22                   != 0   |     OK       | Double error -> uncorrectable (PESEC_UNCORRECTABLE)
  23                   == 0   |     FAIL     | Parity bit itself flipped (PESEC_CORRECTED_PARITY)
  24          
  25               "Parity check OK" means: received_P XOR parity(received_25) == 0.
  26               "Parity check FAIL" means the overall parity is odd, indicating an
  27               odd number of bit flips (1 flip = correctable single error).
  28          
  29             Dependencies:
  30               rx_decoder.h  ->  rx_compute_syndrome()
  31               rx_types.h    ->  uint8_t, uint16_t, constants
  32          
  33             Portability:
  34               No hardware registers are accessed here.
  35             =============================================================================
  36          */
